{"name":"Backwoods","hex":"#4a6546","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"backwoods","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Partly or wholly uncleared forest, especially in North America.","A remote or sparsely inhabited region, especially in North America; away from big towns and from the influence of modern life."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Pertaining to the backwoods.","Rough, uncouth, coarse, or crude in social matters."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/backwoods"}],"entries":[{"title":"Backwoods (song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Backwoods\" is a song co-written and recorded by American country music artist Justin Moore. It was released in October 2009 as the third single from his self-titled debut album. The song became Moore's second Top 10 hit on the US Billboard Hot Country Songs chart with a peak at number 6 in May 2010."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/b/bf/Justin_Moore_-_Backwoods.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Backwoods_(song)"},{"title":"Backwoods (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Backwoods is a 2008 American horror television film directed by Marty Weiss and starring Ryan Merriman & Haylie Duff. It premiered on June 8, 2008 on Spike TV."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/a/a1/Backwoods_VideoCover.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Backwoods_(film)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/b/bf/Justin_Moore_-_Backwoods.png/250px-Justin_Moore_-_Backwoods.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/b/bf/Justin_Moore_-_Backwoods.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/b/bf/Justin_Moore_-_Backwoods.png/250p